                                Topological sort
                                -----------------
can sorting be applied to the graph ?
    Yes - Topological sorting

to sort graphs, a sorting technique topological sort has been invented. two popular algorithms run on these. 
1. DFS based algorithm
2. kahn's topological sort

DFS bases topological sort:
-----------------------------
A DFS bases topolgical sort is a representation of linear ordering of all the vertices in a graph. The only condition to perform topological sort, is that it should not contain any cycles (DAG).Topological sort is mostly used in the project managements tools such as maven, gradle etc..

while arranging vertices in a linear order, topological sort says that - "in an edge (u,v), the vertex 'u' must be processed before the vertex 'v'"

pseudo code:
-------------
1. in addition to the regular stack, you should take another stack. 
2. push all the processed vertices in the second stack.
3. iterate on the second stack and print all the vertices



